BSP-Yocto-Ampliphy-AM68x-ALPHA2                    2024-02-22
=============================================================

- Linux TI vendor kernel v6.1.69 (based on TI tag 09.02.00.002)
  * Tag: v6.1.69_09.02.00.002-phy2
- U-Boot v2023.04 (based on TI tag 09.02.00.002)
  * Tag: v2023.04_09.02.00.002-phy2
- Yocto 4.0 (kirkstone)

NOTE:
This is an ALPHA release and has not been tested for full functionality. It is
possible that some features are not working or stable. This release will NOT
be supported after the first full BSP release.


Tested Yocto Images:
--------------------

- phytec-headless-image:
  * phyboard-izar-am68x-1
  * phyboard-izar-am68x-2
  * phyboard-izar-am68x-3
- phytec-qt5demo-image:
  * phyboard-izar-am68x-1
  * phyboard-izar-am68x-2
  * phyboard-izar-am68x-3


Build Environment:
------------------

- Ubuntu 20.04 64-bit


New Features:
-------------

- Support for new machines representing 1578.1 and 1582.1 hardware:
  * phyboard-izar-am68x-2 for GP SoCs
  * phyboard-izar-am68x-3 for HS-FS SoCs
- PCIe for -2 and -3 machines
- 1.8v MMC/SD for -2 and -3 machines
- RS485 for -2 and -3 machines
- Bootenv support to select devicetree overlays from Linux


Known Issues:
-------------

For phyboard-izar-am68x-1:
- MMC/SD is limited to 3.3v
- The MCU ethernet is limited to 100 MBit/s and booting is not possible
  due to a phy reset triggered from the MCU domain which is unknown to Linux

For phyboard-izar-am68x-2/3:
- The display backlight PWM is not set to the default value occasionally

For all:
- The MIPI DSI interface has the RGB colors flipped occasionally
- The eMMC is limited to HS200 speed mode
- VDD_CPU_AVS is running at default 800mV
